)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Input Queue Panel -- Overtyping          !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  Type a new value over a field of a job and press Enter.
}
{  PRTY  }A priority, digits only: JES2 is told $TJ with P= the value.
}         JES2 decides which values it takes.
{  C     }A job class, A to Z or 0 to 9: $TJ with C=.
{  DEST  }LOCAL or ANYLOCAL, Rn, RMn or RMTn, or Un: $R with D=.
}
}  PRTY and C stand side by side in one field: type over either part.
}
}  All fields typed are checked first. If one is wrong, nothing is done:
}  the values stay as you typed them and the cursor goes to the wrong one
}  (FIELD NOT NUMERIC, INVALID CLASS, INVALID DESTINATION NAME). Action
}  characters typed in the same Enter as an overtype are not done: type
}  them again afterwards.
}
}  Overtyping needs update access to the job; your own jobs you may
}  always change. Without it: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR JOB.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Input Queue help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHLSM
  &ZUP = ISFHIQ
)END
